<Doc
  title="Support · scrnsvr"
  description="Help with ScrnSvr, and how to reach us."
>
  <h1>Support</h1>
  <p>Questions, problems or ideas: email <a href="mailto:support@scrnsvr.art">support@scrnsvr.art</a> and we'll get back to you. It helps to include your iPhone model and iOS version.</p>

  <h2>Common questions</h2>

  <h3>How does the shield work?</h3>
  <p>Choose the apps you'd like to be more intentional with on the <strong>Shield</strong> tab, then turn the shield on. When you open one of those apps, ScrnSvr's shield appears. Tap it and an artwork opens. After spending a little time with it, you can choose a short break in that app, or simply go back to what you were doing.</p>

  <h3>How do I change which apps are shielded?</h3>
  <p>On the <strong>Shield</strong> tab, tap <strong>Choose Apps</strong>.</p>

  <h3>How do I turn the shield off?</h3>
  <p>On the <strong>Shield</strong> tab, slide the shield off and choose for how long: 1 hour, until tomorrow morning, or until you turn it back on.</p>

  <h3>The shield isn't appearing</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Check that the shield is on in the <strong>Shield</strong> tab and that you've chosen at least one app.</li>
    <li>Check that ScrnSvr still has Screen Time access: in the iPhone <strong>Settings</strong> app, go to <strong>Screen Time</strong>, then <strong>Apps with Screen Time Access</strong>.</li>
    <li>Make sure ScrnSvr and iOS are up to date.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>How do I delete my account?</h3>
  <p>In the app, open <strong>Profile</strong>, tap the settings icon, then <strong>Delete account</strong>. This permanently deletes your account, your @handle and your profile picture. See the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for details.</p>

  <h3>What does ScrnSvr know about the apps I use?</h3>
  <p>Very little. Apple's Screen Time framework hides app names from ScrnSvr, and your selection and usage stay on your iPhone. The <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> explains exactly what we collect.</p>
</Doc>
